  "identity_review": "Forty-four component witnesses resolve to eight forms: four complete handed long rules, one tight quarter-circle corner shared by the 3/6-point impressions, one curved junction shared by both sizes, and separate broad 4-point and fine 2-point corners. Complete long rules retain their observed endpoint arrangements; frame corner extraction boundaries lie just beyond measured tangencies and do not imply visible physical type-metal joints. Four composed frames and25ordinary straight runs remain evidence. Geometric fits compare curve/stroke proportions only and never replace the traced ink. Native Boston rule/map-type comparisons, nine relevant semantic sheets and three rotated-retrieval sheets show no exact existing match. Boston quarter arcs have different proportions and tapered ends; its solid rounded-square, sharp angles and parallel rules are different constructions.",
